                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a9bf32af-9646-3466-85e0-441d8b0fb612",
                        "entry_id": "2d832d4c-069a-387c-beb8-7874a7938204",
                        "glosses": [
                            "widersprüchlicher Sachverhalt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "formal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77365c46-d73b-42cb-adbb-44319b6d2058",
                                "sense_id": "a9bf32af-9646-3466-85e0-441d8b0fb612",
                                "text": "„Eine aufschlussreiche Paradoxie kennzeichnet die Situation: Niemals zuvor stand Rom so sehr am Abgrund und gleichzeitig Hannibal so meilenweit von einem Sieg entfernt.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83280444-6e46-460e-9e21-096215a3a932",
                                "sense_id": "a9bf32af-9646-3466-85e0-441d8b0fb612",
                                "text": "„Die Paradoxie des Rauchens ist, dass man es mit Freiheit und Abenteuer gleichsetzt, obwohl Sucht das exakte Gegenteil davon ist.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "de46f120-8e34-4364-a724-31028598adcc",
                        "source_entry_id": "2d832d4c-069a-387c-beb8-7874a7938204",
                        "source_sense_id": "a9bf32af-9646-3466-85e0-441d8b0fb612",
                        "source_sense_description": "bildungssprachlich: widersprüchlicher Sachverhalt",
                        "target_lang_word": "paradox",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paradox",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de9f32be-bdac-3a5a-a225-00859010feed",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An apparently self-contradictory statement, which can only be true if it is false, and vice versa."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7273cbc5-7808-430a-8568-7ec89f85b8b9",
                                                "sense_id": "de9f32be-bdac-3a5a-a225-00859010feed",
                                                "text": "\"This sentence is false\" is a paradox."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b9b6839-326d-483d-a9aa-a008bffff0c8",
                                                "sense_id": "de9f32be-bdac-3a5a-a225-00859010feed",
                                                "text": "The active sense of living which we all enjoy, before reflection shatters our instinctive world for us, is self-luminous and suggests no paradoxes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96215c5c-5c4e-4357-a47a-03f805241e47",
                                                "sense_id": "de9f32be-bdac-3a5a-a225-00859010feed",
                                                "text": "According to one version of an ancient paradox, an Athenian is supposed to say \"I am a liar.\" It is then argued that if the statement is true, then he is telling the truth, and is therefore not a liar […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "168de379-c9bd-37b9-9254-8bef8e0a2c13",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A counterintuitive conclusion or outcome."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "700e01cb-84b7-41af-94fa-760d0b869bc7",
                                                "sense_id": "168de379-c9bd-37b9-9254-8bef8e0a2c13",
                                                "text": "It is an interesting paradox that drinking a lot of water can often make you feel thirsty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfc64310-bf2c-45c1-a08c-b0edc938f8d3",
                                                "sense_id": "168de379-c9bd-37b9-9254-8bef8e0a2c13",
                                                "text": "The most fundamental paradox is that if we're never to use force, we must be prepared to use it and to use it successfully."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5b15557-9814-3de4-bfb3-75cb29961ea2",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A claim that two apparently contradictory ideas are true."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "033c62c4-8c63-46c3-a8de-452af065e435",
                                                "sense_id": "f5b15557-9814-3de4-bfb3-75cb29961ea2",
                                                "text": "Not having a fashion is a fashion; that's a paradox."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43534e2e-d0fe-42c2-8581-4062c498cf98",
                                                "sense_id": "f5b15557-9814-3de4-bfb3-75cb29961ea2",
                                                "text": "How quaint the ways of Paradox! / At common sense she gaily mocks! / Though counting in the usual way years twenty-one I've been alive, / Yet reck'ning by my natal day, / Yet reck'ning by my natal day, / I am a little boy of five!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "632bb0fe-fa32-39e7-bb91-2dacd1d3b7ed",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thing involving contradictory yet interrelated elements that exist simultaneously and persist over time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad254b78-b7a4-3c9d-b089-ffe936b0f206",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or thing having contradictory properties."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b892ca30-a702-4f23-9833-1793f7cb8da8",
                                                "sense_id": "ad254b78-b7a4-3c9d-b089-ffe936b0f206",
                                                "text": "He is a paradox; you would not expect him in that political party."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3eb908be-c0a3-4e7b-8b30-092a606a7971",
                                                "sense_id": "ad254b78-b7a4-3c9d-b089-ffe936b0f206",
                                                "text": "You are a paradox of bitch and angel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5fcca47d-d99e-3f38-a107-1f12429ca25a",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unanswerable question or difficult puzzle, particularly one which leads to a deeper truth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c1a077e-d7be-4850-98ab-8466a549712a",
                                                "sense_id": "5fcca47d-d99e-3f38-a107-1f12429ca25a",
                                                "text": "And only by dismantling our preconceptions of age can we be free to understand the paradox: How young are the old?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61a08185-2fae-33a6-b7d1-0c0b23f7ff70",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A statement which is difficult to believe, or which goes against general belief."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb43f3a2-ff67-429e-a510-2d96ae9b73db",
                                                "sense_id": "61a08185-2fae-33a6-b7d1-0c0b23f7ff70",
                                                "text": "Ay, truly; for the power of beauty will sooner / transform honesty from what it is to a bawd than the / force of honesty can translate beauty into his / likeness: this was sometime a paradox, but now the / time gives it proof."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "faefd106-f6ba-4e90-aaf6-c73cdbcbad37",
                                                "sense_id": "61a08185-2fae-33a6-b7d1-0c0b23f7ff70",
                                                "text": "they contended to make that Maxim, that there is no faith to be held with Infidels, a meere and absurd Paradox [...]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96deb07c-0777-33a3-9fd7-80c365c2f4be",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The use of counterintuitive or contradictory statements (paradoxes) in speech or writing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21a6abf3-7144-4f2e-9241-3a0061d15ea2",
                                                "sense_id": "96deb07c-0777-33a3-9fd7-80c365c2f4be",
                                                "text": "The need for paradox is no doubt rooted deep in the very nature of the use we make of language."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf5b2f92-b9a7-3a10-9b3e-e36c2cdd83d0",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state in which one is logically compelled to contradict oneself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e4f5df2-2022-4ad4-a081-e8db53a6048b",
                                                "sense_id": "bf5b2f92-b9a7-3a10-9b3e-e36c2cdd83d0",
                                                "text": "Thus, like modern disputants, they aimed either to confute the respondent or to land him in paradox."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5515995b-175f-3017-93fc-785b92e8a89e",
                                        "entry_id": "23df3b07-7455-3bc4-b9ca-dc8ff79a0bf3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The practice of giving instructions that are opposed to the therapist's actual intent, with the intention that the client will disobey or be unable to obey."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7546f8fa-752d-4f24-8dd4-7063535507c9",
                                                "sense_id": "5515995b-175f-3017-93fc-785b92e8a89e",
                                                "text": "Defiance-based paradox is employed so that the family will actively oppose and deliberately sabotage the prescription."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dc0cc15a-1cb2-4a4f-81a6-5bb60d347ad4",
                        "source_entry_id": "2d832d4c-069a-387c-beb8-7874a7938204",
                        "source_sense_id": "a9bf32af-9646-3466-85e0-441d8b0fb612",
                        "source_sense_description": "bildungssprachlich: widersprüchlicher Sachverhalt",
                        "target_lang_word": "caractère paradoxal",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d628500-7cc3-4d2b-ae9b-6ee8cc51f308",
                        "source_entry_id": "2d832d4c-069a-387c-beb8-7874a7938204",
                        "source_sense_id": "a9bf32af-9646-3466-85e0-441d8b0fb612",
                        "source_sense_description": "bildungssprachlich: widersprüchlicher Sachverhalt",
                        "target_lang_word": "paradoxe",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paradoxe",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8bb42561-a358-3bd9-bf56-22e951ea83d2",
                                        "entry_id": "99550172-dc7c-3b4f-879f-63c4b7e5643f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Proposition contraire à l’opinion commune ou à la vraisemblance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "600d56f5-616c-44ce-bf8a-9a632b62fce9",
                                                "sense_id": "8bb42561-a358-3bd9-bf56-22e951ea83d2",
                                                "text": "Les paradoxes sans doute sont aussi des idées communes. Il suffit presque toujours de retourner une vérité banale pour en faire un paradoxe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c574238-8620-42c0-9801-6d4bc52c577d",
                                                "sense_id": "8bb42561-a358-3bd9-bf56-22e951ea83d2",
                                                "text": "Nos amis appellent paradoxe celles de nos pensées qui leur déplaisent, par une espèce de gentillesse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e2f7741-25c6-4f77-a7a9-a8493c95f6fd",
                                                "sense_id": "8bb42561-a358-3bd9-bf56-22e951ea83d2",
                                                "text": "Et c'est là un autre paradoxe de Max Jacob : il n’aimait pas Montmartre. Il se défiait de ses « petits maquereautins pâlots que les romances poétisent stupidement », de ses « petits faussaires » et de ses « petits brigands ». Il préférait l'humanité du Paris ouvrier et bourgeois."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7685552-2ba2-36d0-a1e2-54e3409053c1",
                                        "entry_id": "99550172-dc7c-3b4f-879f-63c4b7e5643f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Proposition qui contient ou implique une contradiction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c992244c-e971-4436-97c0-bec32a04cc93",
                                                "sense_id": "a7685552-2ba2-36d0-a1e2-54e3409053c1",
                                                "text": "Là-dessus, nous sombrâmes dans une longue discussion totalement dépourvue d’intérêt, au cours de laquelle nous échangeâmes un bon nombre de paradoxes et de contrevérités."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e9b94ca-0e4f-4250-8142-fc49d59dd5cf",
                                                "sense_id": "a7685552-2ba2-36d0-a1e2-54e3409053c1",
                                                "text": "Il sera prêt à tout donner à l’autre, à tout autre, sauf à donner à cet autre la parole, sa parole. Pathétique aberration : des narcisses prêts à tout donner et ne donnant rien. Ces paradoxes se retrouvent à tout bout de champ dans le social."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e179d97-cb3c-40ec-bce6-07dcc3e15e2d",
                                                "sense_id": "a7685552-2ba2-36d0-a1e2-54e3409053c1",
                                                "text": "Ambivalence, ambiguïté, dénégation : Robert Misrahi soulève le paradoxe qu'il y a à défendre Israël mais à ne pas défendre qu'Israël se défende si on l'attaque."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d719bfe-d255-4714-b611-45552c0887cb",
                                                "sense_id": "a7685552-2ba2-36d0-a1e2-54e3409053c1",
                                                "text": "L’humanité est actuellement dans un étrange paradoxe, d’un côté elle est obsédée par la sécurité et l’augmentation de l’espérance de vie et de l’autre, elle détruit son environnement et en particulier le sol nourricier, mettant ainsi en péril sa propre survie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0058840f-91ab-4c33-88fa-95e8a74ba205",
                                                "sense_id": "a7685552-2ba2-36d0-a1e2-54e3409053c1",
                                                "text": "En cette rentrée, un livre – « le Monde confisqué » – nous aide à comprendre cette nouvelle donne et cet étonnant paradoxe : comment se fait-il qu’une partie de nos dirigeants parlent encore de « concurrence libre et non faussée » quand l’expansionnisme est de retour ? De « libre marché » quand les géants de la tech, de l’énergie ou du transport bénéficient de quasi-monopoles ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
